Keating described Carnage Park as being a nod to films by Sam Peckinpah and Peter Watkins
that were made in the 1970s, and he built the film around that concept.

13
01:10:12,000 --> 01:10:18,000
The film explores themes of robbery, kidnapping,
hostage, bank robbery, death game.

